 ef26fa9 in the PR).\\nPrivacy note\\nLine 169004 of the uploaded log includes Codex telemetry fields (user.account_id, user.email) copied from Codex stderr. Because --attach-logs commits the log to the target (public) repository, those values became public. Hive Mind should redact user.email= / user.account_id= (and similar) fields from Codex stderr before uploading logs.\\nSuggested fixes\\n\\nDetect degenerate output early: when N (e.g. 200) consecutive identical/near-empty stderr/stdout lines arrive from the tool, stop the run (or interrupt the turn) instead of streaming until the output cap, and stop writing the repeated lines to the log (collapse into … repeated N times).\\nTreat max_output_tokens as a resumable failure: automatically resume the Codex thread (codex exec resume) with a short \\\"continue from the current working tree; previous response was truncated\\\" prompt, reusing the recovery branch, instead of ending the session with a failure comment.\\nBound single-turn size: a single turn with ~125M input tokens over ~10h is very prone to degeneration; split very long sessions into multiple turns/sessions (e.g. by time or cumulative tokens) with the working tree preserved between them.\\nRedact account identifiers from logs before --attach-logs uploads (see privacy note).\\nAuto-apply the recovery/&lt;branch&gt; work on the next solve run of the same PR (or at least mention the recovery branch in the failure comment) so the continuation does not need manual cherry-picking.\\nActivitySign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to commentMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsNo labelsNo labelsTypeNo typeProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actionsOpen in GitHub Copilot app\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n            \\n  Footer\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n        \\n    \\n\\n\\n      \\n        &